 person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Cone</surname><given-names>RD</given-names></name></person-group><year>2000</year><article-title>The Melanocortin-4 Receptor,</article-title><person-group person-group-type="editor"><name><surname>, Cone</surname><given-names>RD</given-names></name></person-group><source>The Melanocortin Receptors,</source><publisher-loc>Totowa, , New Jersey</publisher-loc><publisher-name>Humana Press</publisher-name><fpage>405</fpage><lpage>448</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000668-Huszar1"><label>20</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Huszar</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>1997</year><article-title>Targeted disruption of the melanocortin-4 receptor results in obesity in mice.</article-title><source>Cell</source><volume>88(1)</volume><fpage>131</fpage><lpage>41</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9019399</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000668-MacNeil1"><label>21</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>MacNeil</surname><given-names>DJ</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2002</year><article-title>The role of melanocortins in body weight regulation: opportunities for the treatment of obesity.</article-title><source>Eur J Pharmacol</source><volume>440(2&#x02013;3)</volume><fpage>141</fpage><lpage>57</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12007532</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000668-HaskellLuevano1"><label>22</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Haskell-Luevano</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Monck</surname><given-names>EK</given-names></name></person-group><year>2001</year><article-title>Agouti-related protein functions as an inverse agonist at a constitutively active brain melanocortin-4 receptor.</article-title><source>Regul Pept</source><volume>99(1)</volume><fpage>1</